simplybs: 16 KB-align the aarch64-linux-android shared lib.

Google Play requires every native .so in an API 35+ app to use 16 KB-aligned
LOAD segments (enforced since Nov 2025); Android 15+ devices use 16 KB pages.
simplybs's android link flags do not set this, so libmonero_wallet2_api_c.so
would ship 4 KB-aligned and bounce at Play submission. Add
-Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384 to the aarch64-linux-android LDFLAGS. The gomobile
Go .so already gets the same flag via bind.sh -ldflags.

--- a/simplybs/host/main.go
+++ b/simplybs/host/main.go
@@ -287,7 +287,7 @@
 			"*:*:AS=llvm-as",
 			"*:*:LIBTOOL=libtool",
 			"*:*:ANDROID_NDK_HOME=$NATIVEPREFIX/",
-			"*:*:LDFLAGS=$LDFLAGS -lc -lc++abi -lm",
+			"*:*:LDFLAGS=$LDFLAGS -lc -lc++abi -lm -Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384",
 		},
 	},
 	"x86_64-linux-android": {
